 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "Grep for `interior.*ofFunction` under TauCeti/ finds only these private lemmas. `Symplectic/Hamiltonian/Manifold.lean:139` rebuilds a similar `interior \u2026 = mextDeriv (ofFunction \u2026)` shape locally. LieDeriv.lean only has the general `mlieDerivForm_eq_interior_mextDeriv_add_apply` (line 247), with no one-form evaluation.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Contact/Hamiltonian.lean",
   "fix": "Move both to `TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/DifferentialForm/LieDeriv.lean` (or `DifferentialForm/VectorField.lean`), state them for a general `\u03c6 : SmoothForm I M \u211d 1` or a rough one-form, and make them public.",
   "issue": "`interior_eq_ofFunction` (\u03b9_X \u03b1 = ofFunction (y \u21a6 \u03b1(X y))) and `mlieDerivForm_apply_eq` (line 151, L_X \u03b1 (v) = d\u03b1(X,v) + d(\u03b1(X))(v)) are general facts about any one-form, but they are `private` in the contact file. Neither statement nor proof uses the contact condition.",
   "line": 140
  },
  {
   "evidence": "In the diff, `@[simp]` is on `contactHamiltonianVectorField_neg` and `contactHamiltonianVectorField_one`, and absent from `_const_smul` and `_const`. Both point the same direction as those lemmas, so they cannot loop.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Contact/Hamiltonian.lean",
   "fix": "Add `@[simp]` to `contactHamiltonianVectorField_const_smul` and `IsContactForm.contactHamiltonianVectorField_const`.",
   "issue": "`contactHamiltonianVectorField_const_smul` (X_{c\u2022f} = c \u2022 X_f, no side conditions) and `IsContactForm.contactHamiltonianVectorField_const` (line 261, X_c = c \u2022 R_\u03b1) are normal-form rewrites but have no `@[simp]`, while the parallel `_neg` and `_one` do. So simp normalizes `-f` but not `c \u2022 f` or constants.",
   "line": 161
  }
 ],
